From a98f5bb6d4c1fe4889ab084587ba2e255d60c8f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: primez <mpincoski@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:54:34 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] [WebmReader] Take the PTS offset from the first frame
 of a segment

The parser reads the header of the next block to find the duration of
a frame. After the last frame of a cluster, that read switches to the
next segment, and the session sets the PTS offset of that segment. The
sample reader took the PTS of the last frame of the cluster only after
that, so the frame took the offset of the next segment. The PTS diff
was then one frame wrong until the next seek. YouTube DASH sends VP9
and HDR video as WebM with one cluster per segment.

WebmReader now records the PTS of the first frame it reads after the
offset changes, and the sample reader takes the diff from that PTS.

The test copy of AdaptiveStream keeps the reads in a fixated
initialization segment, as the WebM reader expects.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
